WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.967
The assessment starter asks for one row per product and month.

00:00:03.967 --> 00:00:09.537
The browser version is already complete so you can run it and inspect the result.

00:00:09.537 --> 00:00:16.397
In a student assignment, you can remove part of the SELECT or GROUP BY and ask students to

00:00:16.397 --> 00:00:17.867
finish it.

00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:23.482
After running it, explain the output grain and why a Spark version may need a shuffle for the

00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:27.917
grouping keys. For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:27.917 --> 00:00:33.417
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:33.417 --> 00:00:37.137
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:41.562
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:48.887
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:48.887 --> 00:00:53.042
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project:

00:00:53.042 --> 00:00:57.600
validate the meaning of the result, not only whether the statement executes.
